    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleEnglishComments": "- Code comments must be English.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleRiskVerification": "- Declare tunable risk knobs with # @param and read matching context.params defaults only inside executable handlers or callbacks. Encode invalidation, sizing, exits, and safety behavior directly in Strategy API V2 code.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleConservativeDefaults": "- Encode missing assumptions as conservative code parameters or metadata, not prose outside the generated code.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleIndicatorRunnable": "- Indicator output must be runnable in the QuantDinger Indicator editor and suitable for chart display only.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleIndicatorSignals": "- Do not emit strategy execution columns such as open_long, close_long, open_short, close_short, add_long, add_short, reduce_long, or reduce_short.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleOutputSignalsChartOnly": "- output.signals and output.layers are chart-only annotations, not backtest or live order sources.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleOutputLayers": "- Do not add output.layers by default. Use layers only when the user explicitly asks for zones, channels, support/resistance, invalidation ranges, or premium/discount areas. Prefer plots and output.signals for normal indicators.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleLightChartLayers": "- When layers are truly needed, they must look like lightweight analysis annotations, not blocking panels: short text, no opaque gray fill, opacity <= 0.06 for zones, dashed borders, and labels near the right edge or outside dense candles.",
    "aiAssetAnalysis.copilot.nativeStrategyPrompt.ruleScriptDraft": "- Output must be Python Strategy API V2 code. Declare the universe and subscriptions in initialize(context), use target-based order functions, and attach explicit protection rules to entries.",
